---
const faqs = [
  {
    question: "How long does it really take to set up?",
    answer:
      "Most practices go live in under 20 minutes. We integrate with your existing PMS, pull your patient roster, and generate your branded app in one sitting. No code, no IT ticket.",
  },
  {
    question: "Which practice management systems do you support?",
    answer:
      "We support Dentrix, Eaglesoft, Open Dental, Practice-Web, and most cloud-based PMS platforms. If yours isn\u2019t listed, we\u2019ll build the connector \u2014 typically within 48 hours.",
  },
  {
    question: "Is RetainOS HIPAA compliant?",
    answer:
      "Yes. We are fully HIPAA compliant with SOC 2 Type II certification in progress. All patient data is encrypted at rest and in transit, and we sign BAAs with every practice.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can patients really schedule online 24/7?",
    answer:
      "Absolutely. Your branded app syncs live availability from your PMS and lets patients book, reschedule, or cancel from their phone \u2014 no login required. It works while your front desk is asleep.",
  },
  {
    question: "What about recalls and reactivations?",
    answer:
      "Our recall engine automatically identifies patients past due, overdue, or flagged for treatment and sends personalized SMS, email, or app-push sequences. Practices see 40%+ recall response rates.",
  },
  {
    question: "Do patients need to download an app?",
    answer:
      "Nope. Your RetainOS app lives as a progressive web app (PWA) under your brand and domain. Patients access it via a texted link, QR code in your lobby, or a button on your website.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can I control what modules my patients see?",
    answer:
      "Yes. You toggle every module \u2014 booking, forms, messaging, treatment plans, whitening offers, reviews \u2014 on or off from your dashboard. Roll out features at your own pace.",
  },
  {
    question: "What does pricing look like?",
    answer:
      "Pricing starts at $299/mo per location with unlimited patients and no long-term contract. Enterprise DSO pricing is available for multi-location groups. We also offer a 14-day free trial.",
  },
];
---

<section
  class="bg-paper-50 py-24 lg:py-32"
  itemscope
  itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text-900 sm:text-5xl">
        Frequently asked <span class="italic text-violet-600">questions.</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-text-600">
        Everything you need to know about RetainOS \u2014 and if we missed
        something, our team is a click away.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto mt-16 max-w-3xl divide-y divide-paper-line">
      {faqs.map((faq, i) => (
        <details
          class="group py-5"
          itemscope
          itemprop="mainEntity"
          itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"
        >
          <summary
            class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-lg font-semibold text-text-900"
          >
            <span itemprop="name">{faq.question}</span>
            <svg
              class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-text-600 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180 group-open:text-violet-600"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              viewBox="0 0 20 20"
              fill="currentColor"
            >
              <path
                fill-rule="evenodd"
                d="M5.23 7.21a.75.75 0 011.06.02L10 11.168l3.71-3.938a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-4.25 4.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-4.25-4.5a.75.75 0 01.02-1.06z"
                clip-rule="evenodd"
              />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <div
            class="mt-3"
            itemscope
            itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
            itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"
          >
            <p itemprop="text" class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-600">
              {faq.answer}
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
